      "body": "## Motivation\n\nSome clients replay assistant reasoning as `reasoning`. SGLang currently reads `reasoning_content`, so the template can render an empty reasoning block for that history.\n\n## Modifications\n\nCopy a string `reasoning` value into `reasoning_content` only when the native field is missing or null. An explicit `reasoning_content` keeps precedence, and non-string aliases retain current handling.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThe reasoning-replay regression and scoped formatting pass on the updated branch, including native-field precedence. Earlier checks with the real GLM-5.3-Flash tokenizer restored reasoning in rendered prompts. GPU serving and model evaluation remain unverified.\n\nRun the unit suites with `python -m pytest` and formatting with `pre-commit run --files <changed-files>`.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable. This is a request-history compatibility fix.\n\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39176437977](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39176437977)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39176437869](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39176437869)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39176437901](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39176437901)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n\n",
